// GHCN-D by_year, the one frozen file in that tree: csv/by_year/1750.csv, 11.6 MB, 344,589 rows.
// NOAA's readme-by_year.txt states the by_year files are "updated daily for the entire period of
// record", and every other year confirms it (1763, 1800, 1850, 1950, 2024, 2025 all carry
// yesterday's Last-Modified). 1750 is the exception: it is the bucket's implausible-date bucket --
// 3,570 "stations", almost all Australian, reporting between 17500201 and 17500723, i.e. a century
// before GHCN-D's period of record begins -- so the nightly rebuild skips it and it has not moved
// since 2025-01-14. That makes it the only by_year object that can carry EXACT expected tables,
// and it closes csv x SINGLE_FILE, which the MANY_SMALL ghcnd-usw3 corpus does not cover.
//
// Two variants hold PROVEN-identical rows (sha1 of the csv's post-header bytes equals the gunzipped
// gz's): the uncompressed tree is headered, the csv.gz tree is headerless -- the same systematic
// dialect drift the by_station trees show, carried per-variant via header_row false and positional
// path mappings. Expected tables derived at authoring time by clickhouse local over the scratch
// copy of the same pinned objects.

// corpus: ghcnd-by-year-1750
// reference-variant: ghcnd-by-year-1750-s3-csv-uncompressed-single
// pinned: 1 object, 11608918 bytes (csv) / 1385743 (csv.gz), frozen since 2025-01-14
// oracle: clickhouse local 26.8.1.1309
// oracle-sql: SELECT count() FROM file('1750.csv', CSVWithNames, 'ID String, DATE Int64, ELEMENT String, DATA_VALUE Nullable(Int64), M_FLAG String, Q_FLAG String, S_FLAG String, OBS_TIME String')
// oracle-run: 2026-08-25
// read-shape: aggregate
// max-rows: 1
q01_y1750CountObservations
required_capability: dataset_in_from_command
dataset: ghcnd_1750: "{{corpus}}"
FROM ghcnd_1750 | STATS count = COUNT(*);

count:long
344589
;

